  <releases>
    <release version="2.0.2" date="2026-08-02">
      <description>
        <p>Removed the legacy QtWidgets interface.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>The Qt Quick UI is now the only interface; the old QtWidgets fallback and its build option were removed.</li>
          <li>This also drops the now-unused Qt SVG-Widgets dependency from the build.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.0.1" date="2026-08-02">
      <description>
        <p>Bug fixes and polish.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Fixed the connection status parsing: the server and IP shown during an active session now come from the connect command instead of a status field that does not exist.</li>
          <li>Signing out no longer leaves the interface stuck showing an active connection.</li>
          <li>Failed city/server list fetches no longer leave the loading spinner running forever.</li>
          <li>Notifications are suppressed the first time the tray app starts.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
    <release version="2.0.0" date="2026-08-01">
      <description>
        <p>Complete overhaul: new Qt Quick interface on a rewritten, tested core.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Brand-new interface following Proton's visual language: persistent searchable server list with favorites and recents, connection status card, dark and light themes with live system-theme following.</li>
          <li>Rewritten core: all CLI interaction now flows through a tested library with typed parsers, a connection state machine with a stuck-transition watchdog, and fast status polling during connect/disconnect.</li>
          <li>Port forwarding now works inside the Flatpak sandbox.</li>
          <li>New D-Bus control interface (Connect/Disconnect/Raise); launching a second instance now raises the existing window.</li>
          <li>Quitting with an active connection no longer freezes the interface.</li>
          <li>Crisp icons and flags on HiDPI displays.</li>
        </ul>
      </description>
    </release>
  </releases>

